# Workflow for agents

1. Read the approved plan / existing code near the change.
2. Implement the smallest vertical slice that satisfies the request.
3. Add or update tests first or alongside the change.
4. Compile and run tests; fix until green.
5. Summarize what changed, how it was verified (`mvn test` / `mvn verify`), and any remaining risks or open questions.
6. Do not refactor unrelated code, reformat whole files, or add docs the user did not ask for.
7. Do not create git commits or PRs unless the user explicitly asks.

# Definition of done

- Code compiles on Java 25 with the project’s Maven setup
- New/changed behavior covered by tests
- `mvn test` (and ideally `mvn verify`) passes
- No secrets introduced; API contracts and Flyway migrations consistent
- Comments only where needed for clarity of intent
- Change scoped to the request; unexplained churn avoided

# When stuck

- Prefer asking one precise question over guessing business rules
- If a dependency or Boot 4.1.1 / Java 25 incompatibility appears, document it and propose the smallest compatible fix—do not silently downgrade the stack
